  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "〜たら use for：\n１．もし(if)\n２．〜た後、〜てから、〜たとき(When.../ After...)\n３．本当ではないのこと (If (I) was/could/would...., )\n４．勧め(advice/suggestions) (Why don't (you/we)...)",
      "html": "〜たら use for：<br/>１．もし(if)<br/>２．〜た後、〜てから、〜たとき(When.../ After...)<br/>３．本当ではないのこと (If (I) was/could/would...., )<br/>４．勧め(advice/suggestions) (Why don't (you/we)...)",
      "credits_raw": "誠",
      "content_sha256": "394e656b6308ab6303351e11d67dd00410b54683e05551ac892c637392e7e5fe",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Formed like the plain past -ta form with ra added.\n目覚める (mezameru) -> 目覚めたら (mezametara)",
      "html": "Formed like the plain past -ta form with ra added.<br/>目覚める (mezameru) -&gt; 目覚めたら (mezametara)",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "6e426b7c475ca6a0a4bc092df5e185eb9c2ca802b45f5f506f538f1b725bac20",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "'If' type words like もし can be used to make the if/when distinction clear.",
      "html": "'If' type words like もし can be used to make the if/when distinction clear.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "9a3159b54003f769f3e1fffc40b45deda6b9f1b86303880a4d219da907c65c29",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "#5254 もしまず here is wordy. Also, it is always 読んだら、not 読んたら、.\nまず説明書を読んだら、／もし説明書を読んだら、would be better.",
      "html": "#5254 もしまず here is wordy. Also, it is always 読んだら、not 読んたら、.<br/>まず説明書を読んだら、／もし説明書を読んだら、would be better.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "6c8e169f5424033c034b6883de4c1c47c8844acb4a653cb5d878c872a49bc69c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Note that it is unnatural to use -tara in circumstances in the past, where a volitional element is present. For example, if you wanted to say 'I stayed in an old ryokan when I went to Kyouto':\n\n京都に行ったら、古い旅館に泊まりました\n\nThis sentence is unnatural. Using ~tara in the past would only be used for states or circumstances, e.g.\n\n教室に入ったら、小さなネコがいた",
      "html": "Note that it is unnatural to use -tara in circumstances in the past, where a volitional element is present. For example, if you wanted to say 'I stayed in an old ryokan when I went to Kyouto':<br/><br/>京都に行ったら、古い旅館に泊まりました<br/><br/>This sentence is unnatural. Using ~tara in the past would only be used for states or circumstances, e.g.<br/><br/>教室に入ったら、小さなネコがいた",
      "credits_raw": "bi-ru",
      "content_sha256": "9bae5d59b31c09163546965fba8a86d5674f0ce8d4ab7d6084f2496300c4d506",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Maybe the following would be more natural:\n「京都に行ったとき、古い旅館に泊まりました。」\n「教室に入ったとき、小さなネコがいた。」",
      "html": "Maybe the following would be more natural:<br/>「京都に行ったとき、古い旅館に泊まりました。」<br/>「教室に入ったとき、小さなネコがいた。」",
      "credits_raw": "誠",
      "content_sha256": "6f8d5044bba6bd84f80647499a0fc00b7d782888adb9a64a07b5b72fb9c58c98",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "教室に入ったら、小さな猫がいた。is fine enough. You cannot say which is more natural.",
      "html": "教室に入ったら、小さな猫がいた。is fine enough. You cannot say which is more natural.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "5634cd70891bd9c289430d265bc133793e0bf374ef303c7e35559e5dd1b79f12",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "[#5897} Should use the subjunctive mood, not simple past: \"If I were a bird...\"",
      "html": "[#5897} Should use the subjunctive mood, not simple past: \"If I were a bird...\"",
      "credits_raw": "cacepi",
      "content_sha256": "cb55977c9cd9ce66d0dd9e58c68b37bf455b93ad21e281c2a6d4a2c034668218",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "そうそう。確か高校の時に、そう習いました。",
      "html": "そうそう。確か高校の時に、そう習いました。",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "5189a97002cd56f52debfda192ad550115ce543cbb2d836997fed8bd6a95aeb3",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Actually, the past tense usage of たら is okay, as long as the second phrase shows an uncontrollable situation.\n(BAD) 京都に行ったら、古い旅館に泊まりました。\n(GOOD) 先生の説明を聞いたら、すぐ分かった。",
      "html": "Actually, the past tense usage of たら is okay, as long as the second phrase shows an uncontrollable situation.<br/>(BAD) 京都に行ったら、古い旅館に泊まりました。<br/>(GOOD) 先生の説明を聞いたら、すぐ分かった。",
      "credits_raw": "Mukade",
      "content_sha256": "b55d47d1ff50b8801ec54bdcf58e65d0ac53670dbb293795bae9dfeba9d0a87a",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
  ],
